Default curve: maybe set a sensible default so enabling works out of the box. KisCurveOptionData has strengthValue etc. Defaults fine.

Mixin params:
- `edgeWidth` (int, 0-100, default 30): portion of radius considered edge.
- Maybe `edgeContrast`/hardness? Keep two: edgeWidth and `softness`? Keep minimal: edgeWidth only. Actually "边缘扩散" (edge diffusion) — the strength curve controls diffusion amount. One extra param edgeWidth is good. Maybe also `darkenInterior`? Skip.

Now check KisCurveOptionData / KisOptionTuple / KisPrefixedOptionDataWrapper to write the data class correctly. Also check KisPaintOpOptionUtils::loadOptionData. Let me read KisCurveOption.h and KisCurveOptionData.h.

